{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>ערומים.</b> An adjective form, likewise ובגדי ערומים תפשיט (Job 22:6). Some say that ערום ראה רעה ויסתר (Proverbs 22:3) is like it as well, its meaning being that the spirit is naked without covering, like the shape of the letter ayin." "<b>יתבששו.</b> From בושה, and it is of the doubled [forms] in which a nun is hidden between them, and the final letter is doubled, like יתבונן (Job 11:11). And the shin takes a kamatz because it is the end of the verse."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:55.670978210Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}